From: taengu <7606218+taengu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:39:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Parser: a spawn reusing a mob's entity id names the new NPC

The embedded-spawn scan passed over any id already known as a mob, so a
boss spawning under an id an ordinary mob had before kept the old code:
Ritualist Garshim (2100077) spawned as 29091, once a 2920174, and the
meter never showed his fight. It now skips only a spawn naming the code
already stored for that id.
---
 src-tauri/src/capture/stream_processor.rs | 114 ++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 71 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src-tauri/src/capture/stream_processor.rs b/src-tauri/src/capture/stream_processor.rs
index 33e1ec1..7d40dba 100644
--- a/src-tauri/src/capture/stream_processor.rs
+++ b/src-tauri/src/capture/stream_processor.rs
@@ -958,7 +958,14 @@ impl StreamProcessor {
                 if real_id > 1_000_000 {
                     real_id = (real_id & 0x3FFF) | 0x4000;
                 }
-                if !self.data_storage.is_mob(real_id) {
+                // Already read (this spawn's own frame), unless it names
+                // another NPC: the game reuses entity ids, and Ritualist
+                // Garshim (2100077) spawned as 29091, an id a mob (2920174)
+                // had before, so the meter never knew him and showed none of
+                // his fight (2026-10-27).
+                let id_len = read_varint(data, i + 2).length.max(0) as usize;
+                let named = spawn_mob_code(data, i + 2 + id_len).map(|(code, _)| code);
+                if !self.data_storage.is_mob(real_id) || (named.is_some() && named != self.data_storage.mob_code(real_id)) {
                     self.parse_summon_spawn_at(data, i + 2);
                 }
